     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print(cosmo.H0)\n",
    "print(cosmo.get_hmf_grid())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Calculate Radial Kernels $W_X$\n",
    "\n",
    "To calculate the radial kernels $W_X$ in the Limber integration, one has to first specify a cosmology. Once both `Survey` and `Cosmology` are setup, **make sure to compute the window before moving forward**. \n",
    "\n",
    "Below we show how the kernels look like for the galaxy sample. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
<<<<<<< HEAD
